<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="realism-tuning" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> content/tuning.json, crates/engine/src/tuning.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The chosen setting: restart delays at the sourced medians, contest levers, fouls and the booked-player factor, decision weights and carry window, shot weights and noise, the refitted xG fit, and the new corner-source chance. The card chance per foul, the save curve and the hold share do not change.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tuning</td><td>+55 / -50</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, decision.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A new corner source: a pressured clearance or a cross clearance near the defenders' own goal line can go off the defender at a wide angle. A corner still needs a real crossing of the goal line after a defending touch.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>play</td><td>+70 / -7</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/corner_source.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Scenes that prove the corner source gives a corner only after a defending touch over the goal line, and gives none at 0.0.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>tests</td><td>+160 / -0</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> defending.rs, tempo_and_restarts.rs, engine-cli calibrate.rs and moved pins</summary><div class="pl-card">The ten formations against 4-4-2 are judged on 2.4 to 3.2 goals per match. The three tempo tests become gating. The all-suites test gates equal and strength and prints formations. Moved expectations are re-derived and recorded.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tests</td><td>+73 / -64</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> e2e/tests (match-day, first-match)</summary><div class="pl-card">A new seed only if a seed stops scoring in time.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>e2e</td><td>+6 / -6</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> docs/reference/data-files.md, build book run analysis</summary><div class="pl-card">The new values and the regenerated run analysis.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs</td><td>+40 / -20</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>No setting passes every gated band on five seeds (high).</strong> The loop measures every gated figure on every candidate. If no setting passes, the slice stops and reports the closest result and the conflicting pair. No band is widened.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>Goals and the red-card cap are linked (high).</strong> Goals are tuned before the final red-card check.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-danger"><strong>The ten formations against 4-4-2 are far out (high).</strong> They run in the loop from the start.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>The corner source moves other bands (medium).</strong> It lands at 0.0 first, then is tuned with the rest.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Seeded browser tests stop scoring (medium).</strong> A seed is changed only when it fails, and the change is recorded.</aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs">
    <summary>Prior revisions (0)</summary>
    <ul><li>No prior revision.</li></ul>
  </details>
